Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Chrome Enterprise policies for silent, dialog-free printing.
; Review before applying — this affects ALL Chrome profiles on this machine,
; not just the Packing Station kiosk window.
;
; SilentPrintingEnabled: skips print preview entirely, prints straight to
;   the default printer (falls back to auto-saving in Downloads if the
;   default printer is a PDF printer, instead of prompting).
; PrintPreviewUseSystemDefaultPrinter: makes Chrome use the actual Windows
;   default printer, instead of whichever printer was most recently used.
;
; To apply: double-click this file and accept the UAC prompt.
; To undo: delete the two values under this registry key, or set both to 0.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome]
"SilentPrintingEnabled"=dword:00000001
"PrintPreviewUseSystemDefaultPrinter"=dword:00000001
